WEBVTT

00:00:02.690 --> 00:00:03.850
Naenia!

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:07.690
Get away from her, now!

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:09.320
Naenia?

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:12.190
Oh my, is that your name?

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:15.360
That's simply what they call me.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.080
Is it now?

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:21.830
Never mind that. Sit.

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:24.500
The food is here, Noé.

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:35.590
What <i>is</i> this?

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:37.340
She...

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:39.430
No, that <i>thing</i>...

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:43.930
It took Louis from me!

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:45.690
Mademoiselle Chloé.

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:49.770
Are you the Beast of Gévaudan?

00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:54.780
Rumor has it, the Beast
is a curse-bearing vampire.

00:00:54.780 --> 00:01:00.160
If so, then that thing, Naenia,
has robbed you of your true name.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:05.160
How can you sit right
next to her with a smile?

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:07.880
Because it is what I wanted.

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:10.500
What?

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:14.210
It was the price for my wish.

00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:18.140
I became a curse-bearer
of my own free will.

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:21.350
For a wish?

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:23.600
That's right.

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:26.480
There are some names
I'm just dying to have.

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:30.520
But with vampires as powerful as Chloé,

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:34.360
I can't simply take their names by force.

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:37.070
So I politely ask,

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:43.410
"Would you give me your
true name if I grant you a wish?"

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:46.210
The same is true for you, Noé.

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:51.540
I've tried so many times but
have failed to obtain your true name.

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:53.670
You're quite the challenge.

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:58.630
That is why I must ask you, too.

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:00.430
Tell me, Noé.

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:06.730
What wish is worth the price
of giving me your true name?

00:02:06.730 --> 00:02:09.400
Did you...?

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:13.270
Did you say the same to Louis, too?

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:16.820
Louis, is there something I can do?

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:19.780
What can I do to help you?!

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:23.160
Noé...

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:25.740
I... am...

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:35.300
What the hell are you?!

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:37.260
What do you want?!

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:41.340
Why are you doing this?!

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:43.220
Why steal true names?!

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:44.390
Stop this!

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:47.220
Stop stealing them!

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:50.350
Give him back. Now!

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:55.360
Give Louis back to Domi and me!

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:06.370
Listen to me.

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:10.040
I don't care for children who waste food.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:40.210
"The Case Study of Vanitas"

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:48.010
Why'd you have to do that?

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:49.470
Forgive me.

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:51.640
Chloé gets scary when she's mad.

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:52.640
Remember that.

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:55.060
Where is Mademoiselle Chloé now?

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:57.310
She's with that black shadow.

00:04:57.310 --> 00:04:59.980
You should stay away for now.

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:01.320
I know, but...

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:05.110
We cannot allow her to
remain with that dangerous--

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:11.450
You dump food on the floor,
yet your stomach growls?

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:14.040
I truly am sorry.

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:17.670
This was left over.

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:19.710
You can help clean up.

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:32.970
Did you make this?

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:34.100
I did.

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:37.310
And you mended my clothes, too?!

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:38.150
That's right.

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:39.690
How extraordinary!

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:41.730
You're extraordinary, Jean-Jacques!

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:43.860
Is there nothing you can't do?

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:47.360
This is so delicious! It truly is!

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:49.740
R-Really?!

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:52.160
There's nothing extraordinary about it.

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:55.910
I've simply been tending
to Chloé's needs all this time.

00:05:55.910 --> 00:05:58.620
I can't cook or sew to save my life.

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:00.750
Hat's off to you!

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:05.590
Listen, I wish to thank you, Jean-Jacques.

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:09.930
You saved Murr and me, but I never
expressed my gratitude till now.

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:12.100
I must beg your forgiveness once more.

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:14.970
I'd like to make a proper introduction.

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:18.640
My name is Noé.

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:20.100
What's the hand for?

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:21.110
Huh?

00:06:21.110 --> 00:06:24.360
If you want more soup, get it yourself.

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:27.440
I wanted to shake your hand.

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:35.870
No one's ever asked to shake my hand.

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:46.130
How much do you know
about the House of d'Apchier?

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:49.880
Only what was in the dossier you gave me.

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:54.470
Their family line died out in
the aftermath of the Beast's rampage.

00:06:54.470 --> 00:06:57.520
Yeah, but there's more.

00:06:57.520 --> 00:07:01.310
The d'Apchiers were conducting
research on the World Formula,

00:07:01.310 --> 00:07:03.810
even though the Church forbade it.

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:08.110
Their work produced the Alteration Engine,
a device for altering the World Formula.

00:07:08.110 --> 00:07:12.950
That is what gave rise
to the Beast of Gévaudan.

00:07:12.950 --> 00:07:16.040
So the question is what
should or can be done?

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:19.910
Is that why both vampires and
humans are so interested in this?

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:21.620
Most likely.

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:24.880
So, where did you hear all this?

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:27.920
Whose orders are you acting under?

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:32.050
Sir Francis Varney,

00:07:32.050 --> 00:07:35.760
aka the Clockwork Fiend Marquis Machina.

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:37.560
I see.

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:41.560
Marquis Machina tasked me
with getting you involved in this,

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:46.320
no doubt because you are
a member of the Blue Moon Clan.

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:51.400
He also wants to know whether
the Alteration Engine really exists.

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:55.490
And if possible,
I'm to find it and bring it to him.

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:05.250
Herman d'Apchier,
the last head of the family,

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:09.170
his wife, their children,
and his siblings...

00:08:09.170 --> 00:08:11.970
They are all dead.

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:17.350
The only remaining member
of the d'Apchiers is Chloé.

00:08:17.350 --> 00:08:22.520
Jean-Jacques, how long has
Mademoiselle Chloé been here?

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:24.440
She was always here.

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:27.520
Long before the Beast of
Gévaudan reared its head,

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:33.400
Chloé was here watching over each
generation of the d'Apchier family.

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:36.950
Why are you and your people here?

00:08:36.950 --> 00:08:39.790
Are you here to do Chloé harm?

00:08:39.790 --> 00:08:43.160
My enemy is Naenia, not Chloé.

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:47.670
Yet you seek to take that
black shadow away from her.

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:49.460
Naturally!

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:53.670
Who knows what might happen to
Mademoiselle Chloé if nothing is done?

00:08:53.670 --> 00:08:57.050
Van-- I mean, my traveling
companion may have the power

00:08:57.050 --> 00:09:00.060
to restore Chloé's true name.

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:01.470
I will bring him here and--

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:03.140
To do what?

00:09:04.180 --> 00:09:09.270
Are you sure it's a good idea to
leave Noé and that boy together?

00:09:09.270 --> 00:09:12.740
Yes, it is a rare opportunity.

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:16.990
Jean-Jacques should have a friend or two.

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:23.830
Chloé said it was her choice
to have her true name taken.

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:28.210
She had been crying every day
until that shadow appeared.

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:31.800
There was nothing I could do.

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:38.300
I absolutely can't stand when someone
touches what's mine without asking.

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:41.810
You're very mature, aren't you?

00:09:41.810 --> 00:09:44.350
Not at all.

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:47.520
If that is what Chloé wishes,

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:52.980
and it keeps her from weeping,
I'll make peace with it.

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:58.360
I shall be with Chloé till the very end,
even if it means oblivion.

00:09:59.570 --> 00:10:05.000
You may not see it,
but I am a terribly jealous woman.

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:15.010
The scars left by Babel
finally began to fade

00:10:15.010 --> 00:10:18.590
in the latter half of the 16th century.

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:20.800
Listen to me, Chloé.

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:27.060
No one outside these walls must
ever learn that you are a vampire.

00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:28.980
Yes, Father.

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:32.440
I awoke one day to
find that I was a vampire.

00:10:32.440 --> 00:10:35.820
I believe once Babel rendered
the World Formula unstable,

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:39.610
it began having an effect
on this world, too.

00:10:40.990 --> 00:10:44.240
Don't worry. Everything will be fine.

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:49.330
I <i>will</i> make you human again.

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:52.670
Yes, Father.

00:10:52.670 --> 00:10:57.460
My body stopped aging after I turned 11.

00:10:57.460 --> 00:11:01.430
People were told that Chloé
d'Apchier had fallen ill and died.

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:05.970
From that day, the d'Apchiers'
Vampire was hidden away.

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:10.060
At our castle deep in the mountains,

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:17.030
my father gathered renowned mages
and alchemists to study the World Formula.

00:11:17.030 --> 00:11:23.240
Don't worry. It will be all right, Chloé.

00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:28.580
I will make you human again.

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:37.760
Make Chloé d'Apchier human again...

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:44.890
My father's last wish gradually
transformed with the passage of time.

00:11:44.890 --> 00:11:47.510
Unlocking the mysteries
of the World Formula

00:11:47.510 --> 00:11:51.640
and laying hands upon that which
had only been within God's power

00:11:51.640 --> 00:11:55.310
became the House of
d'Apchier's ardent wish.

00:11:55.310 --> 00:11:57.980
I was witness to it all.

00:11:57.980 --> 00:12:00.440
I watched over them.

00:12:00.440 --> 00:12:03.610
I lived among generations of d'Apchiers.

00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:10.000
So you're the legendary Chloé d'Apchier?

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:12.710
You're a vampire, aren't you?

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:15.170
In this day and age,

00:12:15.170 --> 00:12:20.510
you should not let that word so
readily pass your lips, young lady.

00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:21.670
Forgive me.

00:12:21.670 --> 00:12:28.010
You are no longer of the age where
"mademoiselle" is fitting... madame.

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:31.730
He introduced himself as August.

00:12:31.730 --> 00:12:36.610
I had never met another vampire before.

00:12:36.610 --> 00:12:39.780
A key element in
researching the World Formula

00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:43.490
is what to use as the
medium for tampering with it.

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:46.990
The d'Apchier family
chose sound as their medium.

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:48.080
I see.

00:12:48.080 --> 00:12:50.410
You came without even knowing that?

00:12:50.410 --> 00:12:54.460
Does your ignorance know no bounds, boy?

00:12:56.290 --> 00:13:01.300
Forgive me. Was it rude not
to address you as monsieur?

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:05.260
Bravo, Chloé!

00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:07.930
I believe we shall be fine friends!

00:13:07.930 --> 00:13:08.930
Friends?

00:13:08.930 --> 00:13:14.390
If an Alteration Engine that rewrites
the World Formula is truly possible,

00:13:14.390 --> 00:13:18.520
we could turn this world
toward a brighter future!

00:13:18.520 --> 00:13:20.480
The world?

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:27.320
This castle and the mountains of
Gévaudan surrounding it had been my world.

00:13:27.320 --> 00:13:33.330
I knew nothing of the world beyond
that and had not given it any thought.

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:36.500
Outside these walls,

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:41.710
vampires are locked in a violent struggle
with humans, or should I say, the Church.

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:44.840
Throughout the land,
Vampires are being hunted down.

00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:50.260
Even humans are being tortured
to death over mere suspicions.

00:13:50.260 --> 00:13:55.600
In the eyes of the Church, vampires
are an abomination worthy only of death.

00:13:55.600 --> 00:14:00.690
Whose side are you on,
the vampires or humans?

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:03.530
I'm on neither side.

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:05.610
Listen to me, Chloé.

00:14:05.610 --> 00:14:10.030
I am just as fond of vampires
as I am of humans.

00:14:10.030 --> 00:14:14.330
That is why I seek to end the
struggle between them at all costs.

00:14:14.330 --> 00:14:16.830
That is all I wish.

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:22.880
He spoke his mind in his own words.

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:25.590
I envied him for that.

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:27.630
In time, my friend went away,

00:14:27.630 --> 00:14:32.350
and I found myself
eagerly awaiting his return.

00:14:32.350 --> 00:14:35.850
My name is Jeanne! It's nice to meet you!

00:14:35.850 --> 00:14:39.940
There is an assembly I wish
to attend with this child's parents.

00:14:39.940 --> 00:14:42.860
I'd like to place her
in your care for now.

00:14:46.690 --> 00:14:48.360
Stop that, Jeanne!

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:50.820
Come back. We mustn't be outside.

00:14:50.820 --> 00:14:54.370
I spotted a most wonderful
place from my window.

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:56.910
Let's go together, Chloé!

00:15:01.130 --> 00:15:04.000
No, wait.

00:15:19.520 --> 00:15:22.100
Jeanne?! Where are you?!

00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:28.190
Got you!

00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:54.720
It was the first time
I ignored my father's bidding

00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:58.470
and was embraced by the
scents of earth, wind, and flowers.

00:15:58.470 --> 00:16:03.270
It was the first time I saw the
sky so big, blue, and beautiful.

00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:07.570
Everything about that day
was so extraordinarily new.

00:16:13.160 --> 00:16:18.080
I'll look forward to the day when
I can see how you've grown, Jeanne.

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:19.870
Mm-hmm.

00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:31.880
So it was that August took
Jeanne back to her parents.

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:34.550
I haven't heard from her since.

00:16:38.680 --> 00:16:42.020
I worried that something
had happened to her,

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:45.480
but I could not go see her.

00:16:47.480 --> 00:16:50.730
I cannot abandon my family.

00:16:50.730 --> 00:16:54.990
Even though humankind
may very well abandon you?

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:00.450
Chloé.

00:17:03.370 --> 00:17:05.040
August!

00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:11.630
Chloé, how fares your research?

00:17:11.630 --> 00:17:12.590
What?

00:17:12.590 --> 00:17:16.010
Is the Alteration Engine complete?

00:17:18.100 --> 00:17:21.020
I was wrong.

00:17:21.020 --> 00:17:24.020
I thought they could be reasoned with.

00:17:24.020 --> 00:17:28.980
But they cannot.
I was wrong from the start.

00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:32.570
As such, I must set things right.

00:17:32.570 --> 00:17:37.410
But to do that, Chloé,
I shall need the d'Apchiers' research!

00:17:39.070 --> 00:17:40.700
No.

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:43.790
You can't have it, August.

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:56.550
N-No, stop!

00:17:56.550 --> 00:17:59.680
Don't do this, August!

00:18:03.310 --> 00:18:05.140
Swear to me.

00:18:05.140 --> 00:18:13.280
Swear you will use that power of yours,
the knowledge of d'Apchiers, as I command!

00:18:17.530 --> 00:18:20.160
Begone from here, August!

00:18:20.160 --> 00:18:24.580
Each head of the d'Apchier family
pinned his hope upon this research.

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:28.120
It is the whole reason I remain here!

00:18:40.300 --> 00:18:43.760
Chloé, I...

00:18:48.390 --> 00:18:54.940
That was when I lost
my very first friend forever.

00:18:55.990 --> 00:19:00.910
I would later receive a letter from
one who claimed to be August's friend.

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:06.330
That was when I learned the war
between human and vampire kind was over.

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:10.420
The letter said the main architect
of the peace was August.

00:19:10.420 --> 00:19:14.460
He had done all he could to
ascend all the way to the Senate.

00:19:14.460 --> 00:19:18.880
It seems you achieved
your dearest wish, August.

00:19:18.880 --> 00:19:25.060
So it was that I continued my
research alone, decade after decade.

00:19:31.100 --> 00:19:34.110
I wonder if Jeanne is doing well.

00:19:35.360 --> 00:19:38.320
This won't do. I mustn't lay about here.

00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:41.820
I must complete the
Alteration Engine soon.

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:44.700
Then again, to what end?

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:46.120
Why do I do this?

00:19:46.120 --> 00:19:48.620
You're lonely, aren't you?

00:19:48.620 --> 00:19:50.830
You're so lonely, you can't help it.

00:19:50.830 --> 00:19:53.540
You'd do anything to escape that.

00:19:53.540 --> 00:19:58.300
It would have been better if you
had never known the outside world

00:19:58.300 --> 00:20:00.550
or the beautiful blue sky.

00:20:00.550 --> 00:20:05.760
That way, you would have
never known how alone you truly are.

00:20:05.760 --> 00:20:08.060
You must've realized by now.

00:20:08.060 --> 00:20:11.690
Gévaudan is a cage that locks you away.

00:20:11.690 --> 00:20:14.690
You must destroy it
if you wish to end your solitude.

00:20:14.690 --> 00:20:15.520
Stop.

00:20:15.520 --> 00:20:17.780
--Bare your fangs, not your wings.

00:20:17.780 --> 00:20:18.440
--Stop this.
--Bare your fangs, not your wings.

00:20:18.440 --> 00:20:20.860
--Stop this.
--Don't be a little bird.

00:20:20.860 --> 00:20:22.700
Become a beast.

00:20:22.700 --> 00:20:24.370
Enough!

00:20:28.290 --> 00:20:30.040
Jeanne?

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:39.670
Yes, that's right. Near Les Hubacs.

00:20:39.670 --> 00:20:42.300
I heard a young maiden was killed.

00:20:42.300 --> 00:20:45.800
They say her name was Jeanne.

00:20:45.800 --> 00:20:51.520
Her entrails had been devoured,
perhaps by a wolf or some other beast.

00:20:54.480 --> 00:20:58.820
No, that was just a nightmare.

00:20:59.860 --> 00:21:01.940
Which one is the nightmare?

00:21:01.940 --> 00:21:05.490
Me or the world in which you live?

00:21:08.410 --> 00:21:13.330
Poor little Chloé, what is it you wish?

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:16.790
Lonely little Chloé,
what would you like to do?

00:21:16.790 --> 00:21:17.460
--Enough.

00:21:17.460 --> 00:21:18.840
--Tell me.
--Enough.

00:21:18.840 --> 00:21:20.550
Enough.

00:21:20.550 --> 00:21:22.590
What do you truly wish?

00:21:22.590 --> 00:21:24.680
Enough!

00:21:26.470 --> 00:21:29.510
At last, the time has come.

00:21:29.510 --> 00:21:33.270
My wish will finally be granted.

00:21:44.820 --> 00:21:50.450
So, you really will go
through with this, Chloé?

00:21:52.750 --> 00:21:55.250
What the hell's that light?!

00:21:55.250 --> 00:21:58.920
Now I have you, Chloé d'Apchier.

00:22:00.710 --> 00:22:05.010
"The d'Apchiers' Vampire"

00:23:37.020 --> 00:23:41.500
"The Beast"
